<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25365" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάνδῐχα</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδιχα</span>
			, <i>two ways,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μερμηρίζειν</span> halt <i>between two
				opinions,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.189
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ δὲ δ. δῶκε</span> endowed
			thee <i>by halves,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				9.37
			</span></i>; in tmesi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ δ᾽ ἄνδιχα θυμὸν ἔχουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ δ᾽ ἄνδιχα ἔαξα</span>
			broke it <i>in twain,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.256
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1109
			</span></i>; once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κλῇθρα κλίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					1029
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. νηὸς
			ἰούσης,</span> perh. <i>with sails and oars,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.934
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
